const body = `<h1>Unit 10 — Jam Season</h1>

<p class="lesson-lead">Two three-week jams — a two-button constraint jam and a card game jam — teach shipping under deadline. The card jam is the list/data-structure jam: the starter's GameManager ships with Shuffle() and AI_Turn() empty, for you.</p>

<h2>Lessons</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>ID</th><th>Title</th><th>What you build / learn</th></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/10.1a.html">10.1a</a></td><td>2-Button Jam: Kickoff &amp; Pitch</td><td>the constraint; two verbs; scope rules</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/10.1b.html">10.1b</a></td><td>2-Button Jam: Build Day 1</td><td>core loop first — both verbs working</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/10.1c.html">10.1c</a></td><td>2-Button Jam: Build Day 2</td><td>the riskiest task, one system, the first ramp</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/10.1d.html">10.1d</a></td><td>2-Button Jam: Playtest</td><td>three rounds, one fix, verified</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/10.1e.html">10.1e</a></td><td>2-Button Jam: Polish</td><td>juice, three sounds, the freeze and the build</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/10.1f.html">10.1f</a></td><td>2-Button Jam: Showcase &amp; Retro</td><td>arcade row, star votes, the honest retro</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/10.2a.html">10.2a</a></td><td>Card Jam Kickoff: Lists &amp; Arrays</td><td>the six lists in the starter's GameManager</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/10.2b.html">10.2b</a></td><td>ScriptableObjects: Card Data as Assets</td><td>cards you create by clicking, not coding</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/10.2c.html">10.2c</a></td><td>Decks: Shuffle, Draw &amp; Traverse</td><td>Fisher-Yates fills the empty method; render by index</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/10.2d.html">10.2d</a></td><td>Turn Logic: Selection + Iteration</td><td>AI_Turn: the exam's algorithm, assembled</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/10.2e.html">10.2e</a></td><td>Card Jam: Build + Playtest</td><td>win condition, balance pass, three matches</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/10.2f.html">10.2f</a></td><td>Card Jam: Showcase</td><td>rematch demands — and the bridge to the Create PT</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Concepts this unit owns</h2>
<p>Jams are <strong>process tests</strong>: scope, freeze, playtest ritual, and one-fix discipline — and the card jam's lists, procedures, and algorithms ARE the Create PT's requirements, pre-built. CED: AAP-1/2/3, DAT-1, CRD-2.</p>
<h2>Reference docs in this unit</h2>
<ul>
    <li><a href="lists-arrays.html">Lists & Arrays</a> — the list reference: shuffle, traverse, 2D grids</li>
    <li><a href="scriptable-objects.html">ScriptableObjects</a> — data as assets — the card pipeline</li>
</ul>

